      "message": "Looking at some of these functions, I think most of them can instead be done using the power signals, maybe treating some as a pseudo signal from the board specific handlers e.g have PWR_ALL_POWER_GOOD, or a control signal PWR_ASSERT_RSMRST_TO_CPU.\n\nThis area of extending functionality to chipset or board specific handlers needs a better deisgn so that it is not going to be a mess of config items and confusing duplicate functions.\nI\u0027d really like to understand the requirements here. Perhaps someone from Intel could write-up a short doc that covers exactly what the requirements are here, something that outlines:\n - what is \u0027core\u0027 functionality and signals\n - what extensions/functions are needed for individual chipssets (ADL, MTL)\n - How to incorporate platform specific differences (PMIC, discrete etc.)\n\nThen I think we can consider how to design a system that meets these requirements (i.e extensible without being a tangled mess).\nMaybe there\u0027s a doc that covers these requirements already, but I haven\u0027t seen it.\n",
